+**Keep on top.** `setAlwaysOnTop( windowId, true )` paints the window above every window that is not kept on top, including one focused or opened after it; the user does the same with the pin in the title bar (the built-in `core/always-on-top` control). Several windows can be kept on top at once, and among themselves they stack in focus order. Focus is unchanged: the window the user clicked is the focused one (`getFocused()`, `isFocused()`, the focus events) even while a kept-on-top window paints over it. A child window follows its owner, so a child opened from a kept-on-top window stays above it, and child windows get no pin of their own. Fullscreen still wins over everything. The flag is part of the window's session entry and survives a reload; each change fires `os-window-changed` with `reason: 'always-on-top'`. Read it back from `win.alwaysOnTop`.
